# 18. What are dependencies?

A dependency is another package that a package needs to work properly.

Imagine:

```text
My Python Project
       ↓
    requests
       ↓
    urllib3
       ↓
    other dependencies
```

When we install a package, pip can install the required dependencies too.

This is one of the reasons package managers are useful.

---

# 19. `requirements.txt`

A very important concept in Python projects is:

```text
requirements.txt
```

It contains the packages required by a project.

Example:

```text
requests==2.32.3
flask==3.1.0
beautifulsoup4==4.12.3
```

Instead of manually installing every package, someone can run:

```bash
python -m pip install -r requirements.txt
```

The `-r` means:

> Read the package requirements from this file.

---

# 20. Real-world example — Team project

Imagine you create a Python project.

Your project uses:

```text
requests
flask
beautifulsoup4
```

You give the project to your friend.

Your friend doesn't have these packages installed.

Instead of saying:

```text
